      "help": "Usage: ai-analyze [OPTIONS]\n\n  Analyze database schema via LLM and generate business YAML config.\n\n  Uses the v4 Contract-Driven Self-Healing architecture (AutoHealOrchestrator)\n  by default. The legacy Stage3Validator path has been removed (Phase 4 of v4\n  migration).\n\n  Modes:\n    - Full database: sqlseed ai-analyze --db app.db -o config.yaml\n    - Partial tables: sqlseed ai-analyze --db app.db --tables orders,items -o config.yaml\n    - No dependencies: sqlseed ai-analyze --db app.db --tables orders --no-dependencies -o config.yaml\n    - Merge mode: sqlseed ai-analyze --db app.db --tables orders -o config.yaml --merge\n    - Stdout: sqlseed ai-analyze --db app.db (no -o, prints YAML to stdout)\n\nOptions:\n  --db TEXT                  SQLite database path\n  --url TEXT                 Database URL (alternative to --db)\n  --tables TEXT              Comma-separated table names (default: all tables)\n  -o, --output PATH          Output YAML file path (default: stdout)\n  --no-dependencies          Skip FK dependency resolution (analyze only\n                             specified tables)\n  --max-depth INTEGER RANGE  Max FK recursion depth (default: 5)  [x>=0]\n  -m, --model TEXT           AI model name (default: auto-select based on\n                             backend)\n  --api-key TEXT             AI API key (env: SQLSEED_AI_API_KEY)\n  --base-url TEXT            AI API base URL (env: SQLSEED_AI_BASE_URL)\n  --timeout FLOAT            API call timeout in seconds (0=auto, default: auto)\n  --log-llm                  Log full LLM interactions (prompt + response) to\n                             JSON files under <cache_root>/ai_logs/. Useful for\n                             debugging LLM hallucinations and Rule failures.\n  --max-retries INTEGER      Max retries for failed table analysis (default: 2).\n                             On failure, the table is retried with a fresh LLM\n                             call up to this many times.\n  --merge                    Merge newly generated tables into existing YAML\n                             (instead of overwriting). Only tables specified by\n                             --tables are replaced; others are kept. Useful for\n                             re-generating specific tables without re-analyzing\n                             the entire database.\n  --help                     Show this message and exit.\n"
    },
